  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is likely individuals who are familiar with or find humor in racially charged stereotypes, particularly those who recognize and may mock the 'Black people are naturally good swimmers' trope. The meme's intent to use a harmless-looking studious Black man as a subject for a harmful stereotype suggests it is designed for an audience that either finds such racial caricatures amusing or is aware of the stereotype and engages with it as a joke, potentially reinforcing or normalizing the harmful trope. The audience may also include those who are familiar with Facebook naming conventions and family structure stereotypes, as these are used as non-racist 'baseline' contrasts to the main racist joke. The meme's visual of a young Black man holding a book may appeal to or be understood by an audience that sees him as a relatable or 'normal' figure, making the stereotype more jarring and thus more 'funny' to those who are not directly affected by the racism.",
